{"abstract":"Recent studies have shown that language models pretrained and/or fine-tuned on randomly permuted sentences exhibit competitive performance on GLUE, putting into question the importance of word order information. Somewhat counter-intuitively, some of these studies also report that position embeddings appear to be crucial for models' good performance with shuffled text. We probe these language models for word order information and investigate what position embeddings learned from shuffled text encode, showing that these models retain information pertaining to the original, naturalistic word order. We show this is in part due to a subtlety in how shuffling is implemented in previous work - before rather than after subword segmentation. Surprisingly, we find even Language models trained on text shuffled after subword segmentation retain some semblance of information about word order because of the statistical dependencies between sentence length and unigram probabilities. Finally, we show that beyond GLUE, a variety of language understanding tasks do require word order information, often to an extent that cannot be learned through fine-tuning.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Abdou, Mostafa","Ravishankar, Vinit","Kulmizev, Artur","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-474762"],"event":{"acronym":"ACL","end":"2022-05-27","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2022-05-22","title":"60th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, ACL 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"word order does matter i and shuffled language models know it i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2022.acl-long.476","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-474762","identifier":[{"id":"85137729006","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-87f8cfda-c2e1-492a-818f-00fb2df6dc3f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3C14E0D7DE10B7DE21A4A699E3EE1517"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2022.acl-long.476","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341489515/Word_Order_Does_Matter.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mostafa","key":"abdoupau","last":"Abdou","locid":"6dd73bc7-0a10-4cc3-82da-59400ef3ec0d","name":"Abdou, Mostafa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vinit","key":"ravishankarpau","last":"Ravishankar","name":"Ravishankar, Vinit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Artur","key":"kulmizevpau","last":"Kulmizev","name":"Kulmizev, Artur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Smaranda","key":"muresanpedh","last":"Muresan","name":"Muresan, Smaranda","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Preslav","key":"nakovpedh","last":"Nakov","name":"Nakov, Preslav","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Aline","key":"villavicenciopedh","last":"Villavicencio","name":"Villavicencio, Aline","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2022.acl-long.476","eisbn":["9781955917216"],"pages":"6907-6919","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL)","status":"p","title":"ACL 2022 - 60th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics, Proceedings of the Conference (Long Papers)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137729006"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-87f8cfda-c2e1-492a-818f-00fb2df6dc3f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Word Order Does Matter : <i>(And Shuffled Language Models Know It)</i>","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-474762","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Since the popularization of the Transformer as a general-purpose feature encoder for NLP, many studies have attempted to decode linguistic structure from its novel multi-head attention mechanism. However, much of such work focused almost exclusively on English - a language with rigid word order and a lack of inflectional morphology. In this study, we present decoding experiments for multilingual BERT across 18 languages in order to test the generalizability of the claim that dependency syntax is reflected in attention patterns. We show that full trees can be decoded above baseline accuracy from single attention heads, and that individual relations are often tracked by the same heads across languages. Furthermore, in an attempt to address recent debates about the status of attention as an explanatory mechanism, we experiment with fine-tuning mBERT on a supervised parsing objective while freezing different series of parameters. Interestingly, in steering the objective to learn explicit linguistic structure, we find much of the same structure represented in the resulting attention patterns, with interesting differences with respect to which parameters are frozen.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ravishankar, Vinit","Kulmizev, Artur","Abdou, Mostafa","Søgaard, Anders","Nivre, Joakim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416016"],"event":{"acronym":"EACL","end":"2021-04-23","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-04-19","title":"16th Conference of the European Chapter of the Associationfor Computational Linguistics, EACL 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attention can reflect syntactic structure if you let it","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/285250505/Attention_can_reflect_syntactic_structure_if_you_let_it_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416016","identifier":[{"id":"85103335926","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-25c82efb-cb82-462c-afb0-b19e95cecd65"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E646286D0391606B6D9E17BD15686D07"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/285250505/Attention_can_reflect_syntactic_structure_if_you_let_it_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vinit","key":"ravishankarpau","last":"Ravishankar","name":"Ravishankar, Vinit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Artur","key":"kulmizevpau","last":"Kulmizev","name":"Kulmizev, Artur","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Mostafa","key":"abdoupau","last":"Abdou","locid":"6dd73bc7-0a10-4cc3-82da-59400ef3ec0d","name":"Abdou, Mostafa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joakim","key":"nivrepau","last":"Nivre","name":"Nivre, Joakim","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781954085022"],"pages":"3031-3045","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"EACL 2021 - 16th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics, Proceedings of the Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103335926"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-25c82efb-cb82-462c-afb0-b19e95cecd65"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Attention can reflect syntactic structure (if you let it)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-416016","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In order to preserve word-order information in a non-autoregressive setting, transformer architectures tend to include positional knowledge, by (for instance) adding positional encodings to token embeddings. Several modifications have been proposed over the sinusoidal positional encodings used in the original transformer architecture; these include, for instance, separating position encodings and token embeddings, or directly modifying attention weights based on the distance between word pairs. We first show that surprisingly, while these modifications tend to improve monolingual language models, none of them result in better multilingual language models. We then answer why that is: Sinusoidal encodings were explicitly designed to facilitate compositionality by allowing linear projections over arbitrary time steps. Higher variances in multilingual training distributions requires higher compression, in which case, compositionality becomes indispensable. Learned absolute positional encodings (e.g., in mBERT) tend to approximate sinusoidal embeddings in multilingual settings, but more complex positional encoding architectures lack the inductive bias to effectively learn compositionality and cross-lingual alignment. In other words, while sinusoidal positional encodings were originally designed for monolingual applications, they are particularly useful in multilingual language models.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ravishankar, Vinit","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-431703"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","end":"2021-11-11","start":"2021-11-07","title":"2021 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of positional encodings on multilingual compression","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2021.emnlp-main.59","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-431703","identifier":[{"id":"85127434675","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3ff520f1-e214-433c-acd9-1694422323c1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-95E3E5BF9776D64F702C05B5CE4ACC25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2021.emnlp-main.59","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/299760923/The_Impact_of_Positional_Encodings_on_Multilingual_Compression.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vinit","key":"ravishankarpau","last":"Ravishankar","name":"Ravishankar, Vinit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2021.emnlp-main.59","pages":"763-777","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2021 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127434675"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3ff520f1-e214-433c-acd9-1694422323c1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Impact of Positional Encodings on Multilingual Compression","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-431703","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Large-scale pretrained language models are the major driving force behind recent improvements in perfromance on the Winograd Schema Challenge, a widely employed test of commonsense reasoning ability. We show, however, with a new diagnostic dataset, that these models are sensitive to linguistic perturbations of the Winograd examples that minimally affect human understanding. Our results highlight interesting differences between humans and language models: language models are more sensitive to number or gender alternations and synonym replacements than humans, and humans are more stable and consistent in their predictions, maintain a much higher absolute performance, and perform better on non-associative instances than associative ones.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Abdou, Mostafa","Ravishankar, Vinit","Barrett, Maria Jung","Belinkov, Yonatan","Elliott, Desmond","Søgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532130"],"event":{"acronym":"ACL","end":"2020-07-10","place":"Online","start":"2020-07-05","title":"58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the sensitivity of language models and humans to winograd schema perturbations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.679","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532130","identifier":[{"id":"85098815351","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e83f4751-0136-4024-8c6a-137b735d17a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-04F15573225DA74F79DDB1AFEAA5313A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258374822/The_Sensitivity_of_Language_Models_and_Humans.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.679","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Machine Learning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Natural Language Processing","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, The Image Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mostafa","key":"abdoupau","last":"Abdou","locid":"6dd73bc7-0a10-4cc3-82da-59400ef3ec0d","name":"Abdou, Mostafa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vinit","key":"ravishankarpau","last":"Ravishankar","name":"Ravishankar, Vinit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"barrettpau","last":"Barrett","locid":"45ecfb6f-78b7-405c-8bce-f8003b822bf9","name":"Barrett, Maria Jung","name_org":"Barrett, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yonatan","key":"belinkovpau","last":"Belinkov","name":"Belinkov, Yonatan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Desmond","key":"elliottpau","last":"Elliott","locid":"8d2b3fbd-3993-4c1f-a661-fe1075081f31","name":"Elliott, Desmond","orcid":"0000-0003-3112-7904","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"5cfea506-104a-4b40-b63b-e29d037159b0","name":"Søgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-5250-4276","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.679","pages":"7590-7604","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 58th Annual Meeting of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e83f4751-0136-4024-8c6a-137b735d17a1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Sensitivity of Language Models and Humans to Winograd Schema Perturbations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532130","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
